# Vue Frontend Rules

## Stack

- Vue 3 with Composition API and `<script setup lang="ts">`
- Vite + TypeScript (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`)
- Node version via root `mise.toml` (`mise install`) — not `.nvmrc`
- Pinia for state management
- Tailwind CSS v4 + daisyUI 5
- Heroicons (`@heroicons/vue`)
- Vitest for unit and component tests

## Structure (module-oriented)

```
frontend/src/
├── app/                 # bootstrap, router, layouts, styles
├── shared/              # cross-cutting (HttpClient, envs, ApiError, shared types)
├── modules/
│   ├── auth/            # LoginView, AuthService, auth.store, useLogin
│   ├── user/            # UserService + user types
│   ├── health/          # HealthService
│   └── home/            # HomeView

frontend/tests/
├── unit/                # service / pure unit tests (mirrors src)
│   ├── shared/
│   └── modules/
└── component/           # Vue component tests (mirrors src)
    ├── helpers/         # mount helpers (component-only)
    ├── app/
    └── modules/
```

## Standards

- Keep domain code inside its module; do not reach into another module's internals except via its public services/types/stores
- Named services: `interface XService` + `const xService: XService = { ... }`
  (`AuthService` / `authService`; same for User, Health, HttpClient)
- Public env via `import { envs } from '@/shared/env/envs'` — never `import.meta.env` elsewhere
- Extract reusable logic into composables inside the module
- Keep components under 200 lines — split if larger
- JWT lives in memory + `sessionStorage` only (never `localStorage`)
- Handle loading and error states in every data-fetching view
- UI copy in Portuguese; identifiers in English

## Testing

- Unit: `frontend/tests/unit/` (mirrors `src/`)
- Component: `frontend/tests/component/` (mirrors `src/`); mount via `mountComponent` from `tests/component/helpers/mount`
- **Every** component test must end with `expectComponentSnapshot(wrapper)` and commit `__snapshots__/`
- Update snapshots intentionally (`npm run test:component -- -u`) when UI changes are expected

## API Calls

- All HTTP goes through `HttpClient` in `shared/http`
- Domain calls live in `modules/{domain}/services/{Name}Service.ts`
- Use composables to wrap service calls with loading/error state
- Inject auth via `HttpClient.configure` from the auth store in `app/main.ts`
- Never log tokens or OTP codes
